cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "atomipy web module: a visual builder for molecular systems"
message: "If you use the atomipy web module in your research, please cite it using the metadata below, together with the atomipy library it is built on."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Holmboe
    given-names: Michael
    email: michael.holmboe@umu.se
    affiliation: "Umeå University, Sweden"
version: "0.5.1"
date-released: 2026-06-25
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/mholmboe/atomipy-web-module"
url: "https://github.com/mholmboe/atomipy-web-module"
abstract: >-
  A node-based visual programming environment for building, manipulating and
  analysing molecular systems in the browser, built on the atomipy Python
  library. Systems are assembled through a graph interface, and energy
  minimisation and molecular dynamics can be run from the same interface using
  either OpenMM or a local GROMACS engine with the MINFF and CLAYFF force
  fields.
keywords:
  - molecular modelling
  - molecular dynamics
  - clay minerals
  - force field
  - topology
  - MINFF
  - CLAYFF
  - GROMACS
  - OpenMM
  - web application
references:
  - type: software
    title: "atomipy: Atomistic Topology Operations in Python"
    authors:
      - family-names: Holmboe
        given-names: Michael
    repository-code: "https://github.com/mholmboe/atomipy"
